## Goal
Make `scripts/build-app.sh` refuse a build directory that lies inside the repository, including when it gets there through a symlink. A `.app` built inside the repository gets registered with Launch Services.

## Problems
None.

## Decision
The script already rejected an `$OUT` that textually started with the repository root. A symlink outside the repository could still point inside it and slip past that check. After `mkdir -p` and `pwd -P` resolve the path, the same check runs again on the resolved path.

If the directory did not exist before the call, the script removes the one it just created before exiting with an error. A failed run therefore leaves nothing behind in the repository. Directories that already existed are never removed.

`scripts/test-install.sh` gets a regression test. It creates a symlink in a temp directory that points to `internal`, then runs `build-app.sh` with `PORTERO_BUILD_DIR` set to a path under that link. It expects a non-zero exit and checks that `internal/x` was not left behind, cleaning it up if it was.

## Rejected
None.

## Touched
`scripts/build-app.sh`, `scripts/test-install.sh`, `PORTERO_BUILD_DIR` environment variable, macOS Launch Services (the reason for the check).
